{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments ["<b>He brought me</b> — YHWH brought me into His pavilion, in righteousness He brought me. (In visions of Elohim He brought me to the land of Israel. He brought me into the house of wine. He brought me, the King, into His chambers.) This is what the Sages expounded: a maidservant at the sea saw what Ezekiel did not see, and this is 'in visions of Elohim He brought me' — all of them were prophets and merited vision. And so at Sinai: 'He brought me into the house of wine,' i.e., to Mount Sinai, and gave me the Torah, which is expounded in seventy faces. 'He brought me into His chambers' — and showed me the heavens and the heaven of heavens."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 9, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-12T19:09:14.958316096Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}